# Git Branch Policy

- Always work on the `Haider` branch for this project.
- Before making changes, verify the current branch is `Haider` (`git checkout Haider` if not).
- Never commit or push directly to `main`, `Hussain`, or `Jawad` unless the user explicitly requests it.

# Auto-Commit Policy

- After every change you make, automatically commit and push to `Haider`.
- Do not wait for the user to ask — commit immediately once a logical unit of work is done.
- Use clear commit messages describing what changed and why.
- Stage all relevant changed files with `git add`, then `git commit`, then `git push origin Haider`.
- A Cursor hook also auto-commits any remaining uncommitted changes when an agent session ends.
